WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:08.820
We all have those things that grab our&nbsp;
attention, things that stick with us

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:22.300
quite often those things are abstract [Music]

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.480
But when I grow tired of numbers and symbols&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.140
there's one thing that I&nbsp;
keep coming back to [Music]&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:48.060
the camera keeps me grounded in reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:54.480
to really be mindful and see the world&nbsp;
and this campus not only for what it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:01.800
but for what it could be. To capture the&nbsp;
poetry in the things that we walk by every day

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:12.300
A Century of yearbooks by Technique&nbsp;
have inspired me along the way

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:25.380
and to give back and so I joined only to find&nbsp;some things fell through the cracks after the&nbsp;pandemic,

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:32.100
no more office, no official home for&nbsp;
the gear and computers we lend out,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:40.320
nowhere for the old books except a dark room condemned&nbsp;for asbestos. I really don't know what I'm doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:46.980
but I feel like we could bring it all back if&nbsp;
we could get the name out there again and keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:52.500
on taking photos and sharing the joy in looking&nbsp;at things just that little bit more carefully [Music swells]

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:36.720
Technique faces challenges but whatever&nbsp;happens I hope we can get people to think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:43.380
of the Institute not just as a place&nbsp;
to work, but as an infinite canvas

